{"units": [{"id": "pipto-note56", "translation": "And elsewhere πέσε γαίῃ [fell to the ground], yet what Aeschylus and Sophocles wrote as ΠΕΔΟΙ can with equal right be taken for πέδοι [on the ground], as we showed under πέδοι."}, {"id": "pipto-note57", "translation": "Εἰ γὰρ θανόντι νὺξ ἐπ᾿ ὀφθαλμοῖς [For if night upon the eyes of the dead]"}, {"id": "pipto-note58", "translation": "Πίπτον δ᾽ ἐπ᾿ [And falling upon]"}, {"id": "pipto-note59", "translation": "Improperly"}, {"id": "pipto-note60", "translation": "where the scholiast says: εἰ δέ τι ἀνυσθῇ τῷ νεύματι τοῦ Διὸς, ἀσφαλῶς πίπτει καὶ εὐσχημόνως. τὸ γὰρ ἐπὶ νώτῳ πίπτειν τοὺς παλαιστὰς ἄσχημόν ἐστιν [if anything is accomplished by the nod of Zeus, he falls safely and gracefully; for falling on the back is disgraceful for wrestlers]."}, {"id": "pipto-note61", "translation": "With ἐπί [upon] and the accusative"}, {"id": "pipto-note62", "translation": "Τὸ δ᾽ ἐπὶ γᾶν ἅπαξ [And the phrase 'upon the earth' once]"}, {"id": "pipto-note63", "translation": "With πρός [toward]"}, {"id": "pipto-note64", "translation": "Βρέτη [images]"}, {"id": "pipto-note65", "translation": "Ἵπ-πους δινεῖ θελούσας πρὸς πύλαις [He whirls the willing horses toward the gates]"}, {"id": "pipto-quote1", "translation": "to fall dishonored, unbearable falls"}, {"id": "pipto-quote2", "translation": "boastings"}, {"id": "pipto-quote3", "translation": "child"}, {"id": "pipto-quote4", "translation": "having fallen"}, {"id": "pipto-quote5", "translation": "having fallen"}, {"id": "pipto-quote6", "translation": "I will make him fall"}, {"id": "pipto-quote7", "translation": "fallen because of another's wife"}, {"id": "pipto-quote8", "translation": "to kick a fallen man more"}, {"id": "pipto-quote9", "translation": "having fallen"}, {"id": "pipto-quote10", "translation": "an ill-wedded woman falls instead of a man"}, {"id": "pipto-quote11", "translation": "I add a third"}, {"id": "pipto-quote12", "translation": "having fallen"}, {"id": "pipto-quote13", "tra